<p>Your eyes probably feel like sandpaper after hours of working. There&#8217;s a dull pressure behind your temples that wasn&#8217;t there at lunch, and every time you look away from your screen, it takes longer than usual to refocus. Your glasses are fine. You&#8217;ve just been staring at screens since 9 am.</p>
<p>Those are symptoms of Computer Vision Syndrome, or CVS. It covers dry eyes, blurred vision, tension headaches, and neck pain that builds over the course of the day. Remote workers, students, and office staff across Queens and NYC are dealing with it more than ever, and most are managing it with habits that only go halfway.</p>
